      'Rodgers reached Pearl Harbor in August 1945 and departed for Tokyo Bay on 17 August — two days after Japan announced its surrender — arriving on 31 August via Eniwetok and Iwo Jima as the first occupation forces were still organizing ashore. The destroyer that had been built to fight a war arrived just as that war became history, joining the 7th Fleet for the uncertain, consequential work of occupation. The years that followed brought the atomic tests at Eniwetok in 1948, reclassification as a radar picket destroyer, and the full roster of Cold War postings that the Gearing class absorbed.',
