      'On 3 July 1950, Valley Forge made history that no one aboard could have anticipated when the ship was commissioned into peacetime. From her flight deck, F9F Panthers and F4U Corsairs launched the first carrier air strike of the Korean War — strikes against Pyongyang that were also the world\'s first combat sorties by jet aircraft. A carrier built during World War II, commissioned after it, and initially assigned to a peaceful Pacific rotation became in a single morning the instrument of a new kind of warfare. She made four Korean War deployments and earned eight battle stars for that conflict alone.',
